    "updated_at": "2019-08-01T11:52:16Z",
    "body": "Actually, although it's not clearly stated in the spec, the browsers all use the KeyboardEvent.code value, rather than the KeyboardEvent.key value  (see https://www.w3.org/TR/uievents/#events-keyboardevents). But, yes, Firefox's comandeering of the shift key does throw a small spanner in the works.",
